 lose her kiowa  family to confused and angered by her  german family too eager and happy to be  with kid for the rest of her life  still the question remains what exactly  johanna's future truly holds  given that she's essentially the child  of two worlds it would not be hard to  see her as an advocate for native  american rights as an adult  fighting for social justice with her  adoptive father's passion for knowledge  supporting her along the way  even if that's not the path she takes  though she has a bright and loving  future ahead  see all those words put them all  together  you have a story news of the world is  set in 1870 five years after the end of  the american civil war an estate that's  found it particularly difficult to keep  up with the reconstruction era  violent racism remains rampant roads  everywhere are dangerous and people are  willing to do just about anything to  survive or to profit off others  very early on in the film kid tells us  that he's part of this aftermath in no  small way having been a soldier in texas  who didn't surrender until weeks after  the death of abraham lincoln  he is a product of this time and he  suffers for it but of course we know the  history of reconstruction  what the film is more interested in  showing us is an intimate look at the  human cost  because this kid later explains he was  all fighting a war on behalf of other  people and all he got for his trouble  were some scars and the fact that he  wasn't there for the death of his wife  there was a tremendous economic  political and social cost in the  american civil war  some of which we still feel today but it  also left a more human carnage behind  psychological scarring that wasn't  easily healed  news of the world is at its core a story  of two people who have both lost their  family  johanna is as kid eventually learns an  orphaned two times over  having lost her birth parents when she  was too young to really remember them  and then losing her adopted parents at  the hands of people who thought they  were saving her  kid for his part is also without a  family traveling around and making  plenty of friends across texas  even as he refuses to go home to reckon  with the loss of his wife  both of them are on a journey of  reconciliation one that truly picks up  steam when johanna makes a choice  faced with the prospect of rejoining a  group of kiowa who just happened to be  traveling nearby  she instead asked them for a horse  brings it back to kid and keeps  traveling with him  it takes a little longer for kid to  catch up to her emotional wavelength but  the message is clear  this is the moment when she decides that  he is her family and because he  ultimately makes the same choice they  can both find their taste for familial  love again  the entire movie hinges on that choice  when she has to stay rather than to go  and it perfectly sets up the final  moments of the film  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

